1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,100
Every time you write a zero,

2
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:04,253
you're using an
idea from India.

3
00:00:04,293 --> 00:00:07,213
By 2500 BC,
Indus Valley cities

4
00:00:07,253 --> 00:00:11,169
have brick streets
and covered drains.

5
00:00:11,209 --> 00:00:14,509
In 628, Brahmagupta
writes the rules for zero,

6
00:00:14,549 --> 00:00:16,475
as a number of its own.

7
00:00:16,515 --> 00:00:20,335
In 1632, Shah Jahan
begins the Taj Mahal,

8
00:00:20,375 --> 00:00:22,246
in memory of his wife.

9
00:00:22,286 --> 00:00:26,145
By 1858, India is ruled
by the British Crown.

10
00:00:26,185 --> 00:00:28,005
In 1930, Gandhi
marches to the sea,

11
00:00:28,045 --> 00:00:30,494
to make his own salt.

12
00:00:30,534 --> 00:00:33,714
In 1947, at the
stroke of midnight,

13
00:00:33,754 --> 00:00:35,638
India becomes independent.

14
00:00:35,678 --> 00:00:38,118
In 2023, India
becomes the first

15
00:00:38,158 --> 00:00:40,735
to land near the
Moon's south pole.

16
00:00:40,775 --> 00:00:44,395
Today, more than 1.4 billion
people call India home,

17
00:00:44,435 --> 00:00:46,430
more than any other country.

18
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:50,250
What surprised you
most? Tell us below.

